      "answer": "(1) $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$, $b=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ (2) $5$ (3) $-1$",
      "solution": "(1) $z=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{1+i}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}(1-i)}{(1+i)(1-i)}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}i}{2}$ 이므로 $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$, $b=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\n(2) $2z=\\sqrt{2}(1-i)$, $4z^{2}=-4i$, $z^{2}=-i$, $z^{4}=-1$, $z^{5}=-z$이므로 최소의 자연수 $n=5$\n(3) $z+z^{2}+z^{3}+z^{4}+z^{5}+z^{6}+z^{7}=z+z^{2}+z^{3}+z^{4}(1+z+z^{2}+z^{3})=z+z^{2}+z^{3}-(1+z+z^{2}+z^{3})=-1$",
